To create a goal model for the multi-robot system mission, we break down the mission into hierarchical goals and tasks, considering parallel execution and fallback mechanisms for handling battery issues. Here's the structured model:

### Goal Model Table

| Goal ID | Goal Title | Goal Text | Runtime Annotation | Goal Type | Relation | Justification |
|---------|------------|-----------|--------------------|-----------|-----------|---------------|
| G1      | Execute Resource Collection and Delivery Mission | Ensure resources are collected and delivered successfully. | Parallel execution: # | Achieve | - | The mission involves parallel collection and delivery phases. |
| G2      | Resource Collection | Collect required resources from storages. | Parallel execution: # | Perform | OR | Collection and delivery are parallel phases. |
| G3      | Resource Delivery | Deliver collected resources to specified locations. | Parallel execution: # | Perform | OR | Collection and delivery are parallel phases. |
| G2.1    | Attempt Collection | Attempt to collect resources without battery issues. | Fallback(G2.2) | Perform | AND | If battery drops, fallback to reassign. |
| G2.2    | Reassign Collection Task | Reassign collection task due to low battery. | - | Perform | AND | Ensures mission continuation if initial attempt fails. |
| G3.1    | Attempt Delivery | Attempt to deliver resources without battery issues. | Fallback(G3.2) | Perform | AND | If battery drops, fallback to return resources. |
| G3.2    | Reassign Delivery Task | Reassign delivery task due to low battery. | - | Perform | AND | Ensures mission continuation if initial attempt fails. |
| AT1     | Collect Sterile Equipment | Collect sterile equipment from storage. | - | Perform | AND | Single robot assigned for this task. |
| AT2     | Collect Clean Linens | Collect clean linens from storage. | - | Perform | AND | Single robot assigned for this task. |
| AT3     | Deliver Sterile Equipment | Deliver sterile equipment to destination. | - | Perform | AND | Single robot assigned for this task. |
| AT4     | Deliver Clean Linens | Deliver clean linens to destination. | - | Perform | AND | Single robot assigned for this task. |

### Justifications and Relationships

- **G1 -> G2, G3 (OR)**: The mission requires both collection and delivery, which can be executed in parallel, making them independent but both necessary.
  
- **G2 -> G2.1, G2.2 (FALLBACK)**: If the initial collection attempt fails due to low battery, another robot takes over, ensuring the task is completed.

- **G3 -> G3.1, G3.2 (FALLBACK)**: Similarly, if delivery fails, another robot continues, ensuring resources are delivered.

- **G2.1 -> AT1, AT2 (AND)**: Both tasks must be completed for collection to be successful.

- **G3.1 -> AT3, AT4 (AND)**: Both tasks must be completed for delivery to be successful.

This model ensures efficient resource management with fallback mechanisms for reliability.
